From dada8c24bacae3f590f95ddf0be25f9c516dd0f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Raxcoms <mpaulo968@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 23:49:08 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] gamescope: add hooks for an optional external color provider

Load the AutoHDR provider through one versioned C interface. The provider
owns inverse tone mapping, eligibility, color plans, presentation policy
and pipeline retries without Gamescope or graphics-stack dependencies.
Missing or incompatible providers leave native presentation active.

Keep only the host bridge for frame facts, LUT resources and atomic
operations here. Reuse SDR gamut mapping, the LUT builder and native
color-state tracking. The provider maps linear RGB before shared gain,
white balance and output encoding; scanout and composition use the same
extra LUT pair while SDR overlays retain their normal mapping.

Primary/unleased-plane checks and allocation constraints keep the effect
on the game without forcing composition. Disabled processing bypasses
the provider after one-time cleanup. No GPU conversion pass is added.
The interface is independent of private Gamescope layouts; updates still
need review of host hook ordering, layer identity and shader slots.
